[Metro Board file 2026-0783, Motion / Motion Response]
APPROVE Motion by Padilla, Bass, and Sandoval to direct the Chief Executive Officer to:

A.	Prepare a First/Last Mile plan for the Sun Valley Metrolink Station, building on the City of Los Angeles's 2023 motion to study station relocation and a second platform, and coordinated with the Brighton to Roxford Double Track Project. Report back to the Planning and Programming Committee within 60 days on a scope and schedule;

B.	Direct staff to establish early coordination on the design and construction schedule of the Brighton to Roxford Double Track Project with the California High-Speed Rail Authority's Palmdale to Burbank SR14A alignment through Sun Valley. Develop recommendations that preserve design flexibility and experience for riders;

C.	Evaluate options for additional parking around the future Pacoima Metrolink Station and Mobility Hub, including Metro and City controlled parcels;

D.	Confirm whether the East San Fernando Valley Light Rail Transit Project's First/Last Mile Plan for the former Sylmar LRT station remains applicable to the Sylmar Metrolink Station and eligible under Metro First/Last Mile Guidelines for local return and 3% local contribution;

E.	Prioritize Sylmar, Pacoima, and Sun Valley, and their related first and last mile improvements, as essential regional rail infrastructure for competitive state and federal grant funding and Metro's own grant-making capacity, including the Metro Active Transport program, to construct the improvements identified under Items A, and D; and

F.	Report back to the Planning and Programming Committee on the above items B - E in 180 days.
